      <h1>How the Bitcoin Blockchain Works</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">The Bitcoin blockchain is the ordered history of valid Bitcoin blocks selected by accumulated proof of work. Blocks link backward through previous-block hashes, while nodes independently validate each candidate chain. The selected history can change during a reorganization, so confirmation depth matters and first inclusion is not absolute finality.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Network</li><li>Shallow</li><li>Explainer</li><li>10 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-18</li></ul>
      <p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Preview only. Publication records and confirmed URLs do not exist; all navigation remains inactive.</p>
